{
  "summary": "Critical bug fix: Changed parseInt radix from 3 to 10. The original code incorrectly parsed NEZHA_MAX_SESSIONS in base-3, causing values like '10' to parse as 3 in base-3 (which equals 3 in decimal) or fail for digits >= 3.",
  "learnings": [
    {
      "topic": "parseInt radix",
      "reminder": "Always use radix 10 for parseInt when parsing decimal numbers. Other radixes (2-36) are for binary/octal/hex or other bases. Using wrong radix causes silent data corruption."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Environment variable validation",
      "reminder": "When parsing env vars with parseInt, validate the result. Consider using Number.parseInt with explicit radix 10, or add bounds checking (e.g., maxSessionsPerType = Math.max(1, parsedValue))."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Test coverage for constructor edge cases",
      "reminder": "Add tests for constructor parameter parsing, especially for env var defaults and boundary values (0, negative, NaN, very large numbers)."
    }
  ],
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "type": "bug-fix",
      "description": "Radix was 3 instead of 10 - this was a critical bug causing incorrect parsing of NEZHA_MAX_SESSIONS env var"
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "type": "test-coverage",
      "description": "No test verifies the constructor's radix parsing behavior with env vars"
    }
  ],
  "praise": [
    "Good catch on the radix bug",
    "Tests comprehensively cover the core functionality (registerSession, heartbeat, unregister, cleanup)",
    "Good use of transaction blocks in registerSession",
    "Proper error handling with ROLLBACK in catch block"
  ],
  "suggestions": [
    "Consider adding bounds validation for maxSessionsPerType (e.g., reject values < 1)",
    "Add test for constructor with explicit maxSessionsPerType parameter",
    "Consider adding a comment explaining the default value logic"
  ],
  "overallScore": 90,
  "codeQualityScore": 85,
  "testCoverageScore": 80,
  "documentationScore": 75
}

